{
  "id": "m36l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "map y filter",
    "en": "map and filter"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Transformar y filtrar colecciones"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`map(funcion, iterable)` aplica una función a cada elemento; `filter(condicion, iterable)` se queda con los que cumplen. Ambas devuelven iteradores: envuélvelos en `list()`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "nums = [1, 2, 3, 4]",
          "print(list(map(lambda x: x * 10, nums)))",
          "print(list(filter(lambda x: x % 2 == 0, nums)))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[10, 20, 30, 40]",
          "[2, 4]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "En la práctica, una comprensión de lista suele leerse mejor que map/filter, pero conviene conocerlos."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Transforming and filtering collections"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`map(func, iterable)` applies a function to each element; `filter(cond, iterable)` keeps those that pass. Both return iterators: wrap them in `list()`."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "nums = [1, 2, 3, 4]",
          "print(list(map(lambda x: x * 10, nums)))",
          "print(list(filter(lambda x: x % 2 == 0, nums)))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "[10, 20, 30, 40]",
          "[2, 4]"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "In practice a list comprehension often reads better than map/filter, but it's worth knowing them."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m36l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `dobles(numeros)` que devuelva cada número multiplicado por 2 (usa map).",
        "en": "Define `dobles(numeros)` returning each number times 2 (use map)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def dobles(numeros):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def dobles(numeros):",
